WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.355
In many villages,

2
00:00:01.355 --> 00:00:02.118
the barber,

3
00:00:02.118 --> 00:00:03.775
the potter and the carpenter

4
00:00:03.775 --> 00:00:05.273
weren't paid in cash.

5
00:00:05.273 --> 00:00:06.506
They got a share of

6
00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:07.781
the harvest.

7
00:00:08.119 --> 00:00:11.056
William Wiser described it in

8
00:00:11.056 --> 00:00:13.258
1936, from his study of

9
00:00:13.258 --> 00:00:15.500
a village in Uttar Pradesh.

10
00:00:15.838 --> 00:00:17.656
The jajman was the patron,

11
00:00:17.656 --> 00:00:19.579
often a landowning caste.

12
00:00:19.579 --> 00:00:21.425
Service castes were paid in

13
00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:23.603
kind, in long-term ties.

14
00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:26.354
Some saw it as reciprocity.

15
00:00:26.354 --> 00:00:28.142
Others as exploitation,

16
00:00:28.142 --> 00:00:30.304
unequal and hereditary.

17
00:00:30.665 --> 00:00:31.891
Your turn.

18
00:00:31.891 --> 00:00:34.203
What is the patron called?
